From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 10:19:50 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: Add chassis-type to the boards that lack
 it

Fifteen Apple silicon device trees had no chassis-type: the M3 and M4
MacBook Air and Pro, MacBook Air (M5), MacBook Neo, the M3 and M4 iMacs,
Mac mini (M4), Mac mini (M6) and Mac Studio (M3 Ultra). Every other Mac
has it.

Without it the bootloader reports an unknown enclosure in the SMBIOS
tables, and systemd-hostnamed, GNOME and power management cannot tell a
laptop from a desktop. On the MacBook Neo hostnamectl showed no chassis
and /sys/class/dmi/id/chassis_type read 2 (Unknown).

Add "laptop", "desktop" or "all-in-one" as for the other boards of each
kind.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit 05ba7730e2c98accb644775e559635cb6cc1c137)

[j604 backport: t8132-j773g.dts context differs in omacom 7.2.11 (aliases + ramoops); the one chassis-type line placed by hand]
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
